---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '../../data/site';
import { CHILDRENS_FUNERAL_SUPPORT } from '../../data/funding';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Funerals we arrange', url: '/funeral-services/' },
  { name: "Children's funerals", url: '/funeral-services/childrens-funerals/' },
];
---

<Page
  title="Funerals for Babies & Children — East Lothian"
  heading="When a baby or child dies"
  description="Funerals for babies and children in East Lothian, including stillbirth. There is no burial or cremation fee for a child in Scotland, and no charge from us."
  standfirst="There is no charge for this. Not from the council, not from the crematorium, and not from us."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <p>
    We are very sorry that you are reading this page.
  </p>

  <p>
    There is nothing useful anyone can say about why this has happened. What we can do is
    take every practical thing off you, tell you plainly what your choices are, and give
    you as much time as you need to make them. There is no hurry at any stage.
  </p>

  <Callout tone="accent" title="There is no cost">
    <p>
      {CHILDRENS_FUNERAL_SUPPORT.summary} <strong>We make no charge either</strong> — no
      professional fee, no coffin charge, no charge for our cars or our time.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Nobody should be making decisions about their child's funeral with one eye on what
      it costs. If anyone tells you otherwise, please telephone us.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Take your time</h2>
  <p>
    You do not need to decide anything today, or this week. Some families arrange things
    within days because they want it done; others wait a fortnight or more until family
    can travel or until they simply feel able. Both are right. We will keep your baby or
    child safely in our care for as long as you need.
  </p>

  <h2>Being with them</h2>
  <p>
    You can spend as much time with your child as you want, whenever you want, for as
    long as you want. You can hold them. You can bring brothers and sisters,
    grandparents, anyone you would like. You can bring a blanket, a toy, a photograph,
    something you have knitted.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some parents want to wash and dress their child themselves. You can. Some would find
    that unbearable, and would rather we did it. That is right too, and we will do it
    with the same care you would.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some families take hand and footprints, or a lock of hair. If you would like that and
    have not thought to ask, we can arrange it — including afterwards, if it occurs to
    you later.
  </p>

  <h2>Stillbirth and very early loss</h2>
  <p>
    Everything on this page applies equally to a stillborn baby. The hospital will discuss
    your options with you, and you are free to use us rather than the hospital's own
    arrangements if you would prefer — you are entitled to choose, and choosing does not
    cost you anything.
  </p>
  <p>
    For a pregnancy loss before 24 weeks, hospitals in Lothian and the Borders offer
    respectful arrangements including cremation and burial. If you would rather make your
    own, we will help you do that. Please just ask. Nothing about this is too small a
    loss to arrange a funeral for.
  </p>

  <h2>The funeral itself</h2>
  <p>
    Whatever you would like it to be. Some families want a full service in a church.
    Some want six people at a graveside. Some want a short blessing and nothing else. We
    have helped with all of these.
  </p>
  <p>Things families often ask about, and the answer is yes to all of them:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Carrying your child yourself, rather than us doing it</li>
    <li>Brothers and sisters being involved — choosing music, drawing on the coffin</li>
    <li>Colours instead of black, and asking people not to wear dark clothes</li>
    <li>A small white coffin, or a woven willow one, or one you decorate yourselves</li>
    <li>Holding the service somewhere that is not a church or a crematorium</li>
    <li>Having no service at all, and doing something later instead</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Burial or cremation</h2>
  <p>
    Both are free for a child in Scotland. Councils in East Lothian and the Scottish
    Borders set aside particular areas for children's burials, often with different rules
    about memorials that allow more than a conventional grave would — toys, windmills,
    ornaments. We will show you where they are.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you choose cremation, ashes from a baby are sometimes very few or none at all,
    depending on how tiny they were. The crematorium will be honest with you about what
    to expect, and so will we. It is better to know beforehand.
  </p>

  <h2>Financial help</h2>
  <p>
    Beyond the fees that are already waived, Funeral Support Payment is available in
    Scotland for the funeral of a baby or child, including a stillborn baby, if you or
    your partner receive certain benefits. It can be paid straight to us.{' '}
    <a href="/funeral-costs/help-with-funeral-costs/">More about Funeral Support Payment</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Support, whenever you want it</h2>
  <p>
    Not now, necessarily. Perhaps in six months, when everyone else has gone back to
    normal. These organisations are there either way, and we have listed how to reach them
    on our <a href="/bereavement-support/">bereavement support page</a> — including
    baby-loss support in Edinburgh and the Lothians, national stillbirth and neonatal
    charities, and support for bereaved brothers and sisters.
  </p>

  <Callout tone="accent">
    <p>
      Whenever you are ready, telephone{' '}
      <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref} class="font-semibold">{CONTACT.phone}</a>. You will
      speak to one of us. There is no charge for anything, including asking.
    </p>
  </Callout>
</Page>
